FINAL ANSWER:
By surviving lines, **Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own most of the repo.** Neither is active now, apart from two small commits under a second "Troy" email this April.

## Lines in HEAD by author (all 1,997 tracked lines)

| Author | Lines | Share | Active |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | 41% | 2013–2019 (+48 lines in Apr 2026, see below) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | 31% | 2017–2021 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 5% | almost all in `scorecard.yml` |
| Jon Church | 72 | 4% | README |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3% | almost all in `codeql.yml` |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | 3% | CI and release |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | 2% | CI matrix |
| ~25 others | ~230 | 12% | each under 2% |

**In the actual code (`lib/` and `test/`, 1,202 lines), it's even more concentrated:** Troy has 56% and Doug 33%. In `lib/index.js` alone, Troy has 159 of 238 lines (67%) and Doug 22 (9%). Nobody else has more than about 16 lines there.

By file:
- **Mostly Troy:** `lib/index.js`, `test/vary.js` (100%), `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/issue-2.js` (83–86% each), and README (42%).
- **Mostly Doug:** `.eslintrc.yml`, HISTORY.md, LICENSE, and `ci.yml` (54%).
- **Split:** `test/test.js` is about even (Doug 46%, Troy 43%).
- **Recent contributors:** they own the CI, workflow and docs files rather than the code.

## Things that would skew a naive count
1. **The reformat commit.** `62628c0` by Fiona Formatter reformatted all the JS. Plain `git blame` credits Fiona with 291 lines of `lib/` and `test/`, more than Doug gets. I followed the repo's `.git-blame-ignore-revs` and ignored whitespace (`-w`), so those lines go back to whoever actually wrote them. Fiona owns 2 lines in total, the ignore file itself.
2. **Two "Troy Goode" emails.** `<email redacted>` (2013–2019) and `troy@laptop.example` (two commits on 2026-04-10, 48 lines) are counted as one person above. That rests only on the matching name, which anyone can set. If the second email isn't really Troy, his share drops to 38%, and those 48 lines (12 in `lib/index.js`) are owned by an unknown author.
3. **Moved code.** I tracked copied and moved lines (`-M -C`), so code that was moved between files stays credited to its original author.

## What this means
The core library and tests were written by two people who stopped contributing years ago. The current maintainers have mostly written docs, CI and packaging, so no active contributor owns much of `lib/index.js`. If you're planning reviewers or onboarding, that's the area at risk.

Line ownership is a stand-in for knowledge, not a measure of it. Active maintainers who review code but rarely write it won't show up here. There's a busfactor skill in this session, but I didn't use it: it scores weighted commit activity, which is the measure you asked me not to use. I didn't change any files in the repo.

